WEBVTT

00:00:04.280 --> 00:00:06.110
Today I'll go with a normal Lunch Combo A.

00:00:06.110 --> 00:00:10.560
But sneaking out for some Italian
at Saizuriya wouldn't be bad, either!

00:00:22.000 --> 00:00:23.210
What are you after!?

00:00:23.210 --> 00:00:25.120
My life?
My chastity!?

00:00:25.120 --> 00:00:26.880
It's my first time, 
so be gentle!

00:00:25.420 --> 00:00:26.880
Calm down. It's me!

00:00:26.880 --> 00:00:28.130
That voice...

00:00:28.130 --> 00:00:29.250
Is that you, Lucia?

00:00:29.400 --> 00:00:31.320
I'm going to let you go now.

00:00:31.320 --> 00:00:34.100
B-But keep your eyes closed 
until I say it's okay.

00:00:34.100 --> 00:00:35.060
Got it?!

00:00:35.060 --> 00:00:36.190
You have to!

00:00:37.140 --> 00:00:38.010
All right.

00:00:41.020 --> 00:00:42.180
O-Okay.

00:00:42.180 --> 00:00:43.290
Open your eyes.

00:00:46.490 --> 00:00:47.850
I-It's a maid uniform.

00:00:47.850 --> 00:00:49.110
Got a problem with that?!

00:00:50.300 --> 00:00:53.440
Uh, want me to take you to the infirmary?

00:00:53.850 --> 00:00:57.870
You're the one who told me to serve you 
a homemade lunch in a m-maid uniform!

00:00:57.870 --> 00:01:02.580
O-Oh, the maid uniform was obviously a joke.

00:01:05.340 --> 00:01:07.700
I've made a huge mistake!

00:01:07.700 --> 00:01:10.450
Yay, I'm so happy you kept your promise!

00:01:10.450 --> 00:01:12.460
And it looks great on you! So lovely!

00:01:13.360 --> 00:01:14.970
R-Really?

00:01:14.970 --> 00:01:17.080
Yeah, it's super cute.

00:01:17.080 --> 00:01:17.590
Huh?!

00:01:17.760 --> 00:01:19.600
Cu... Cu...

00:01:19.920 --> 00:01:21.720
No!

00:01:21.720 --> 00:01:24.100
You jerk!

00:01:22.700 --> 00:01:24.970
Why?!

00:02:59.030 --> 00:03:04.180
W-Well, since you went to all the trouble,
I'll help myself to your lunch box!

00:02:59.070 --> 00:03:04.070
Episode 6
Occult Club Activity Log

00:03:04.180 --> 00:03:05.030
Sure...

00:03:06.720 --> 00:03:07.790
Wow!

00:03:08.080 --> 00:03:12.580
So this is a girl's homemade lunch,
the stuff of ancient legend!

00:03:12.580 --> 00:03:15.180
Q-Quit being stupid and eat it already!

00:03:15.180 --> 00:03:15.780
Okay.

00:03:15.780 --> 00:03:16.800
Thanks for the meal.

00:03:17.740 --> 00:03:19.200
H-How is it?

00:03:19.200 --> 00:03:21.100
Yeah, it's tasty.

00:03:21.100 --> 00:03:23.430
I love the simple warmth that's 
characteristic of home cooking.

00:03:23.660 --> 00:03:25.060
R-Really?

00:03:25.060 --> 00:03:26.310
Thank goodness.

00:03:29.270 --> 00:03:33.980
But, to be honest, I got Shizuru to
help me make that lunch.

00:03:33.980 --> 00:03:35.100
Shizuru?

00:03:35.100 --> 00:03:36.570
A little, mostly with the seasoning.

00:03:36.840 --> 00:03:38.460
My sense of taste has been abnormal

00:03:38.460 --> 00:03:41.220
ever since my body became this way.

00:03:42.090 --> 00:03:46.010
<i>That's why she was able to eat that
super-spicy parfait like it was nothing?</i>

00:03:46.580 --> 00:03:49.810
Shizuru has helped me out for ages.

00:03:49.810 --> 00:03:51.080
Um, at Guardia—

00:03:51.960 --> 00:03:53.010
Sorry.

00:03:53.010 --> 00:03:57.170
Um, have you been with Shizuru at 
that "G" organization all this time?

00:03:57.170 --> 00:03:57.840
Yeah.

00:03:58.070 --> 00:04:02.730
Shizuru can generate a medicine that 
neutralizes my poison within her body.

00:04:02.730 --> 00:04:05.540
As such, Shizuru has been my one,

00:04:05.540 --> 00:04:07.470
precious friend all this time.

00:04:07.850 --> 00:04:09.830
Your friend, huh?

00:04:09.830 --> 00:04:11.100
So, I'm sorry,

00:04:11.500 --> 00:04:14.520
but I ended up telling her 
about your special power, too.

00:04:15.480 --> 00:04:17.440
Oh, I see.

00:04:18.090 --> 00:04:19.200
Don't worry.

00:04:19.200 --> 00:04:21.700
I have no intention of telling 
anyone other than Shizuru.

00:04:21.700 --> 00:04:24.200
Not Touka-san, or the organization.

00:04:24.680 --> 00:04:28.820
Shizuru's wish is for you 
to lead a peaceful life,

00:04:29.160 --> 00:04:30.930
far from the clutches of the organization.

00:04:31.280 --> 00:04:32.360
I see.

00:04:32.360 --> 00:04:34.020
Shizuru is too kind.

00:04:34.700 --> 00:04:37.030
She <i>is</i> my one and only friend, after all.

00:04:37.030 --> 00:04:37.750
Hey.

00:04:37.750 --> 00:04:38.750
Huh?

00:04:38.750 --> 00:04:40.370
I told you this the other day.

00:04:40.370 --> 00:04:41.760
I'm here now, too.

00:04:41.760 --> 00:04:43.290
Not to mention the occult club.

00:04:44.320 --> 00:04:47.690
Do you think Ohtori-san will forgive me?

00:04:48.050 --> 00:04:49.140
Don't worry.

00:04:49.140 --> 00:04:51.640
She's been wanting to apologize to you, too.

00:04:52.880 --> 00:04:53.860
It's all right.

00:04:54.230 --> 00:04:55.390
I'll be with you.

00:04:57.380 --> 00:04:58.230
Yeah.

00:04:58.600 --> 00:05:00.440
Thanks, Kotarou.

00:05:00.440 --> 00:05:01.250
Sure!

00:05:02.740 --> 00:05:03.900
Did you just call me "Kotarou"?

00:05:05.180 --> 00:05:07.800
Wh-What's wrong with me calling you by name?!

00:05:07.800 --> 00:05:09.980
Wh-Why are you snapping at me?!

00:05:11.170 --> 00:05:13.290
I'm sorry, Ohtori Chihaya!

00:05:13.480 --> 00:05:14.160
Huh?!

00:05:14.160 --> 00:05:16.310
Hey, what's all this?

00:05:16.310 --> 00:05:17.610
It's an apology, of course!

00:05:17.610 --> 00:05:20.360
I am very sorry for being so 
nasty to you the other day!

00:05:20.360 --> 00:05:22.290
That's not what I meant!

00:05:22.290 --> 00:05:26.040
Oh, jeez, what was the point of me
fasting since this morning

00:05:26.040 --> 00:05:29.270
to work up the determination 
to apologize to you?!

00:05:29.270 --> 00:05:30.550
I'm starving!

00:05:30.720 --> 00:05:33.180
Why don't you hurry up 
and apologize too, then?

00:05:33.180 --> 00:05:35.050
You have a point!

00:05:35.050 --> 00:05:36.560
I'm sorry, Konohana-san!

00:05:36.800 --> 00:05:38.510
I was out of line!

00:05:38.510 --> 00:05:41.670
Mhm, it's great that you were 
able to apologize, huh, Chi-chan?

00:05:42.010 --> 00:05:44.140
Here, eat all you like!

00:05:45.820 --> 00:05:47.950
This bread is yummy!

00:05:48.660 --> 00:05:49.840
By the way...

00:05:50.560 --> 00:05:52.700
This has been bugging me since earlier.

00:05:53.520 --> 00:05:54.580
What is it?

00:05:54.580 --> 00:05:57.120
Why have you been clinging 
to him all this time?

00:05:58.010 --> 00:05:59.460
Because we're friends, naturally!

00:05:59.460 --> 00:06:00.690
<i>What do I do with this girl?</i>

00:06:00.690 --> 00:06:03.340
<i>She's oblivious to how much 
distance friends should keep!</i>

00:06:04.550 --> 00:06:06.070
Sh-Shizuru-san?

00:06:06.070 --> 00:06:07.000
What are you doing?

00:06:07.000 --> 00:06:07.890
It's no problem.

00:06:07.890 --> 00:06:09.720
I'm friends with you, too.

00:06:14.990 --> 00:06:16.290
Hey, Lucia-san?!

00:06:16.290 --> 00:06:17.450
What the?

00:06:17.450 --> 00:06:18.730
My arm's getting buried! My arm!

00:06:19.980 --> 00:06:21.890
I can't believe we're so unevenly matched.

00:06:22.200 --> 00:06:23.550
I'm sorry, Kotarou.

00:06:23.550 --> 00:06:25.030
Why are you apologizing?

00:06:25.030 --> 00:06:27.740
I'm pretty sure there's demand 
for chests like yours, too!

00:06:28.840 --> 00:06:32.800
Shizuru, thanks for being considerate 
about the "G" incident.

00:06:32.800 --> 00:06:33.640
Sure.

00:06:33.640 --> 00:06:35.760
I want you to be free.

00:06:36.110 --> 00:06:37.000
I see.

00:06:37.000 --> 00:06:38.120
If that's how it is...

00:06:39.290 --> 00:06:40.160
All right!

00:06:40.160 --> 00:06:43.380
Let's go get some Occult Club work done!

00:06:45.230 --> 00:06:48.730
<i>"Somewhere in Kazamatsuri exists
a legendary, holy sword</i>

00:06:48.730 --> 00:06:50.900
<i>that only a true hero can pull out."</i>

00:06:51.240 --> 00:06:55.260
<i>Someone submitted that info to the blog,
and we went out in search of it!</i>

00:06:55.140 --> 00:06:57.680
<b>Case 1</b>

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.850
<b>Case 1</b>

00:06:57.680 --> 00:06:59.850
<b>The Legend of Kazamatsuri's Holy Sword</b>

00:06:59.980 --> 00:07:00.490
Hey!

00:07:00.490 --> 00:07:01.900
This is just a candy shop!

00:07:02.140 --> 00:07:04.060
Thank you. That will be a million yen.

00:07:04.060 --> 00:07:05.090
Starfish Cutter!

00:07:05.090 --> 00:07:06.150
<i>And they're enjoying themselves!</i>

00:07:06.480 --> 00:07:08.780
Looks like it was a bad lead.

00:07:09.100 --> 00:07:12.030
Kotarou, there's a holy sword right here.

00:07:13.070 --> 00:07:15.530
This is the holy sword, Excalibur!

00:07:15.840 --> 00:07:18.060
They say it's been stuck here
for around ten years,

00:07:18.060 --> 00:07:20.320
and nobody's been able to pull it out yet.

00:07:20.320 --> 00:07:22.040
That's a legend, all right.

00:07:22.040 --> 00:07:23.130
Exactly.

00:07:23.710 --> 00:07:27.420
However, I'll put a full stop
 to that legend today.

00:07:29.870 --> 00:07:30.920
Papagatero!

00:07:30.920 --> 00:07:32.180
Who the hell is that?!

00:07:33.640 --> 00:07:36.150
I don't give a damn about you right now.

00:07:36.150 --> 00:07:38.850
I'll sink these fangs I've been
sharpening for the last ten years

00:07:38.850 --> 00:07:41.660
into this holy sword, right here and now!

00:07:40.400 --> 00:07:41.960
I pulled it out!

00:07:43.020 --> 00:07:44.400
The legend!

00:07:46.150 --> 00:07:48.180
Don't break it!

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.690
<b>Case 1</b>

00:07:48.650 --> 00:07:49.690
<b>The Legend of Kazamatsuri's Holy Sword</b>

00:07:49.690 --> 00:07:51.110
<b>SOLVED</b>

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.410
<b>Case 2</b>

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.410
<b>Panic!</b>

00:07:52.910 --> 00:07:54.410
<b>The Laugh That Echoes From the Darkness</b>

00:08:04.170 --> 00:08:05.170
<b>Thriving Business</b>

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:20.850
<b>Case 2</b>

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:20.850
<b>Panic!</b>

00:08:19.970 --> 00:08:20.850
<b>The Laugh That Echoes From the Darkness</b>

00:08:20.850 --> 00:08:23.940
<b>SOLVED</b>

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:26.810
<b>Case 3</b>

00:08:24.350 --> 00:08:26.810
<b>The Ogre Who Lives in the 
School Building at Night</b>

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:45.960
<b>Case 3</b>

00:08:45.040 --> 00:08:45.960
<b>The Ogre Who Lives in the 
School Building at Night</b>

00:08:45.960 --> 00:08:47.580
<b>SOLVED</b>

00:09:05.270 --> 00:09:09.400
The Dinosaurs Vs.
The Yayoi People

00:09:12.900 --> 00:09:13.860
Kazamatsuri City Hall

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:14.650
<b>The T-Rex Lived Until the 2nd Century!</b>

00:09:13.860 --> 00:09:14.650
<b>Case 4</b>

00:09:14.650 --> 00:09:17.950
<b>SOLVED</b>

00:09:23.700 --> 00:09:26.920
A modern day utopia?
I saw a rainbow paradise
at the Tsumugi River Basin!

00:09:24.590 --> 00:09:29.480
The subject of this weekend's quest is 
this lead which was sent to our blog!

00:09:29.480 --> 00:09:31.600
So basically, a picnic in the forest?

00:09:32.180 --> 00:09:33.490
Sakuya, Sakuya!

00:09:33.490 --> 00:09:36.930
Fill up my lunch box with tamagoyaki
and octopus-shaped wieners!

00:09:37.200 --> 00:09:38.600
Understood.

00:09:38.600 --> 00:09:41.500
I shall prepare lunch boxes for five
on the day of your trip.

00:09:42.010 --> 00:09:43.810
He casually ignored me!

00:09:44.240 --> 00:09:45.180
Not at all.

00:09:45.180 --> 00:09:46.740
Slowtarou-kun, I wanted to give you

00:09:46.740 --> 00:09:50.200
the special opportunity to harvest 
and savor fresh, local ingredients.

00:09:50.200 --> 00:09:52.080
It was a butler's display of consideration.

00:09:52.080 --> 00:09:53.170
Let me see.

00:09:53.170 --> 00:09:56.260
Podostroma and gyromitra mushrooms 
are in season right now.

00:09:56.260 --> 00:09:57.620
I highly recommend them.

00:09:57.620 --> 00:10:00.200
A murder plot that doesn't 
dirty your own hands?!

00:10:00.440 --> 00:10:02.170
A utopia, huh?

00:10:02.470 --> 00:10:05.050
Are you sure it's not just another bad lead?

00:10:05.490 --> 00:10:08.250
No! I want to trust our contributors!

00:10:08.250 --> 00:10:10.880
So, anyone interested, 
please raise your hand!

00:10:10.880 --> 00:10:11.600
Pass.

00:10:11.600 --> 00:10:12.680
I guess I'll pass.

00:10:12.680 --> 00:10:13.590
I'll pass.

00:10:13.590 --> 00:10:14.960
Surprisingly, I'll pass.

00:10:14.960 --> 00:10:16.040
"Ass" indeed.

00:10:16.040 --> 00:10:17.930
Wait a second, you crass butler!

00:10:17.930 --> 00:10:18.690
Yes?

00:10:18.690 --> 00:10:19.850
I...

00:10:23.080 --> 00:10:25.720
Don't let these traitors
pressure you into a decision.

00:10:25.890 --> 00:10:28.230
Come on, tell me how you really feel!

00:10:28.740 --> 00:10:30.050
Kotarou...

00:10:30.050 --> 00:10:31.230
Got it.

00:10:31.760 --> 00:10:34.070
If possible, I don't really 
want to go, either.

00:10:34.760 --> 00:10:35.890
Okay, it's settled!

00:10:35.890 --> 00:10:37.700
Tomorrow, on Saturday, 
we're going on a quest!

00:10:37.700 --> 00:10:38.560
Got it?!

00:10:39.360 --> 00:10:42.200
<i>If we're going to the forest, 
we'll need a bodyguard.</i>

00:10:43.380 --> 00:10:45.200
Sorry, I fell behind schedule!

00:10:46.640 --> 00:10:47.980
You're late, Kotarou.

00:10:47.980 --> 00:10:49.960
You suggested this, so don't be late!

00:10:50.160 --> 00:10:52.300
<i>Lucia's sudden lovey-doveyness
died down, huh?</i>

00:10:52.300 --> 00:10:55.210
<i>Not sure if I should call it a relief
or a disappointment.</i>

00:10:55.210 --> 00:10:56.340
Sorry about that.

00:10:56.490 --> 00:10:57.910
So, what're you up to?

00:10:57.910 --> 00:11:00.980
Kotori brought a dog as a bodyguard.

00:11:00.980 --> 00:11:02.610
It's so cute!

00:11:02.610 --> 00:11:03.970
Wow, a dog?

00:11:06.080 --> 00:11:07.230
Look, Chibi-Moth.

00:11:07.230 --> 00:11:08.920
Say hi to Kota-san.

00:11:08.920 --> 00:11:10.000
Moth!

00:11:10.000 --> 00:11:11.620
Isn't this a mammoth?

00:11:11.620 --> 00:11:14.200
I think I've seen it before in the forest.

00:11:14.200 --> 00:11:16.610
Yes, I did pick him up in 
the forest the other day,

00:11:16.820 --> 00:11:18.620
but as you can see, he's a dog.

00:11:18.620 --> 00:11:20.370
H-He is?

00:11:20.710 --> 00:11:23.200
Chibi-Moth is as strong as they come!

00:11:23.200 --> 00:11:26.120
Yeah, around three Yoshinos, I'd say.

00:11:26.330 --> 00:11:27.880
I feel bad for Yoshino.

00:11:27.880 --> 00:11:32.150
Uh, there's no way he's three times
as strong as Yoshino.

00:11:32.150 --> 00:11:34.350
Chibi-Moth, go all-out for a sec.

00:11:43.030 --> 00:11:44.090
Are you trying to kill me?!

00:11:44.090 --> 00:11:45.220
Sorry.

00:11:45.220 --> 00:11:47.610
But, if he's this powerful,

00:11:47.610 --> 00:11:50.180
he'll be a perfect bodyguard 
for us in the forest.

00:11:51.160 --> 00:11:52.230
Something's sticking out of him!

00:11:52.230 --> 00:11:54.670
Look, this thing's totally a mammoth!

00:11:54.670 --> 00:11:55.480
Huh?

00:11:56.610 --> 00:11:57.850
There's nothing there.

00:11:57.850 --> 00:11:59.590
Did you hit your head or something?

00:11:59.590 --> 00:12:02.240
It's not good to make strange 
accusations just because you lost.

00:12:02.510 --> 00:12:04.960
Kotarou, have the courage to admit defeat.

00:12:04.960 --> 00:12:06.390
Unsightly.

00:12:06.390 --> 00:12:08.590
Forget it. I'm done.

00:12:09.940 --> 00:12:11.670
What did you bring for snacks?

00:12:11.670 --> 00:12:13.010
I've got candy.

00:12:13.010 --> 00:12:14.530
I have salted rice crackers!

00:12:14.530 --> 00:12:15.370
Sweet natto.

00:12:15.370 --> 00:12:16.330
Woffers.

00:12:16.330 --> 00:12:17.380
Woffers?

00:12:17.920 --> 00:12:19.000
These.

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.610
Oh, jam wafers?

00:12:19.000 --> 00:12:20.610
Yeah, woffers.

00:12:20.610 --> 00:12:21.360
Huh?

00:12:21.360 --> 00:12:22.130
Huh?

00:12:22.130 --> 00:12:26.100
Boss, don't you know that stupid girl?
Shouldn't you take her side?

00:12:26.100 --> 00:12:28.890
I didn't see or hear anything.

00:12:30.320 --> 00:12:31.390
What is it?

00:12:31.390 --> 00:12:34.070
Oh, what a pretty river.

00:12:34.070 --> 00:12:36.270
What course are we following?

00:12:36.270 --> 00:12:37.110
Let's see.

00:12:37.110 --> 00:12:38.580
This is where we are.

00:12:38.580 --> 00:12:41.620
From here, we'll take a shortcut through
the forest and head downstream.

00:12:41.620 --> 00:12:43.780
You made sure to look into it ahead of time.

00:12:43.780 --> 00:12:44.990
Of course.

00:12:44.990 --> 00:12:47.810
Right now, I'm a pretty reliable guy!

00:12:48.420 --> 00:12:49.880
How promising.

00:12:49.880 --> 00:12:52.290
I have my full trust 
placed in you, of course.

00:12:52.880 --> 00:12:56.870
Oh no. I dropped my emergency flare.

00:12:56.870 --> 00:12:59.210
You don't trust me in the slightest!

00:13:00.600 --> 00:13:02.460
It looks so clean. I bet it tastes great.

00:13:02.730 --> 00:13:03.970
Stop it.

00:13:03.190 --> 00:13:03.970
Cut it out.

00:13:03.970 --> 00:13:04.800
Huh?

00:13:04.800 --> 00:13:07.860
If you drink the river water raw, 
it'll give you a stomachache.

00:13:08.180 --> 00:13:10.980
It runs through a village upstream,

00:13:10.980 --> 00:13:13.300
so you're better off not drinking it.

00:13:13.300 --> 00:13:17.860
Oh, there could be wastewater mixed in.

00:13:18.670 --> 00:13:20.910
Yes, that could be quite dirty.

00:13:20.910 --> 00:13:21.750
Gulp, gulp, gulp...

00:13:21.750 --> 00:13:22.860
I just said not to drink it!

00:13:23.390 --> 00:13:24.400
Good taste!

00:13:24.650 --> 00:13:27.290
<i>Well, it shouldn't be a problem for Shizuru.</i>

00:13:31.670 --> 00:13:32.790
Annoying.

00:13:32.790 --> 00:13:34.750
You don't like bugs, President?

00:13:34.750 --> 00:13:37.160
<i>Nobody</i> likes them.

00:13:37.160 --> 00:13:41.680
There sure are a lot more bugs once you 
go just a little ways into the forest.

00:13:41.680 --> 00:13:42.800
Obviously.

00:13:42.800 --> 00:13:45.700
They use insecticide around the city

00:13:45.700 --> 00:13:48.300
and the outskirts of the 
forest adjacent to it.

00:13:48.480 --> 00:13:49.300
Huh?

00:13:49.500 --> 00:13:52.030
This is Mother Nature's true form.

00:13:52.030 --> 00:13:54.780
Humans can't deal with it, though.

00:13:55.110 --> 00:13:58.190
You don't want to live in a city 
swarming with insects either, do you?

00:13:58.190 --> 00:14:00.140
Well, that's true,

00:14:00.140 --> 00:14:02.440
but kind of wrong, too...

00:14:02.780 --> 00:14:04.110
It can't be helped.

00:14:04.110 --> 00:14:08.320
Life and living aren't always beautiful.

00:14:08.320 --> 00:14:10.700
People only accept what is beautiful.

00:14:11.070 --> 00:14:15.510
The greenery close to us is fake
and unnatural to the core.

00:14:15.820 --> 00:14:19.210
But couldn't you also call that
a product of human progress?

00:14:19.540 --> 00:14:24.440
Improving our habitat in order to survive
seems only natural to me.

00:14:24.840 --> 00:14:28.470
Even if the things we humans
so arrogantly call "improvements"

00:14:28.470 --> 00:14:32.600
end up causing a fatal error in
the environment and Earth itself?

00:14:33.450 --> 00:14:34.850
Even so, humans will—

00:14:36.350 --> 00:14:37.170
Now, now.

00:14:37.170 --> 00:14:41.510
Calm down, you two, and let's admire 
these Hercules and Caucasus beetles.

00:14:42.030 --> 00:14:44.710
So they live in Japan, too!

00:14:44.710 --> 00:14:46.720
Kazamatsuri is really something.

00:14:49.550 --> 00:14:50.460
You okay?

00:14:50.460 --> 00:14:51.410
Yeah.

00:14:51.410 --> 00:14:54.000
The greenery is just a little thick here.

00:14:54.000 --> 00:14:55.240
Now that you mention it...

00:14:55.660 --> 00:14:58.010
<i>The smell of the greenery is suffocating.</i>

00:14:58.010 --> 00:15:00.500
<i>The bugs disappeared at some point, too.</i>

00:15:00.500 --> 00:15:01.370
A monster!

00:15:02.290 --> 00:15:03.910
An orthrus appeared!

00:15:03.910 --> 00:15:05.500
Wait a second, Shizuru!

00:15:05.500 --> 00:15:07.020
A-A monster?

00:15:07.020 --> 00:15:08.340
Like a raccoon dog?

00:15:08.780 --> 00:15:09.830
Moth!

00:15:10.230 --> 00:15:12.120
I think he's telling us to follow him.

00:15:12.120 --> 00:15:13.040
Got it!

00:15:13.040 --> 00:15:14.580
Lead the way, Chibi-Moth!

00:15:18.540 --> 00:15:21.320
Um, doesn't something smell weird?

00:15:21.320 --> 00:15:22.000
Huh?

00:15:23.550 --> 00:15:25.020
You're right. This is awful.

00:15:26.690 --> 00:15:28.400
Oh, you found them?

00:15:28.400 --> 00:15:29.020
All right!

00:15:40.390 --> 00:15:43.020
<i>This</i> is the utopia?

00:15:43.520 --> 00:15:45.540
Don't get any closer, Kotarou!

00:15:46.670 --> 00:15:47.790
Lucia! Shizuru!

00:15:47.790 --> 00:15:50.670
Jeez, we were worried about you two!

00:15:50.670 --> 00:15:52.930
Never mind. Look at that.

00:15:55.620 --> 00:15:58.610
Kotarou-kun, this used to be a forest.

00:16:00.390 --> 00:16:03.230
Is this a tree that's rotting away?

00:16:03.230 --> 00:16:06.260
Toxins most likely permeated 
all the way into the soil,

00:16:06.260 --> 00:16:08.260
drying up and rotting the forest.

00:16:08.260 --> 00:16:09.650
Kotarou, look at this.

00:16:11.190 --> 00:16:12.340
The orthrus.

00:16:12.750 --> 00:16:14.630
It was alive until just a minute ago.

00:16:14.630 --> 00:16:16.170
It was walking and everything.

00:16:16.170 --> 00:16:17.780
But now...

00:16:18.810 --> 00:16:21.150
The UMAs in Kazamatsuri...

00:16:21.150 --> 00:16:24.930
Don't tell me the unidentified animals 
we've been hearing about have all been...

00:16:24.930 --> 00:16:26.370
It appears the toxins

00:16:26.370 --> 00:16:29.540
that seeped into the ground 
caused birth defects.

00:16:29.540 --> 00:16:31.870
Was it caused by wastewater?

00:16:31.870 --> 00:16:33.170
Most likely.

00:16:33.170 --> 00:16:35.300
So, what will you do?

00:16:35.620 --> 00:16:37.810
Didn't you come here to investigate this?

00:16:37.810 --> 00:16:38.930
Well...

00:16:39.930 --> 00:16:42.780
Orthrus, rest in peace.

00:16:43.360 --> 00:16:44.310
Anman.

00:16:44.310 --> 00:16:45.440
"Amen," right?

00:16:47.020 --> 00:16:49.480
Okay, let's go home before it gets dark.

00:16:51.180 --> 00:16:54.000
Kotarou-kun, you didn't take a picture?

00:16:54.000 --> 00:16:55.070
I guess not.

00:16:55.070 --> 00:16:56.220
Are you sure?

00:16:56.220 --> 00:16:58.680
Wouldn't "We found the 
source of the monsters"

00:16:58.680 --> 00:17:01.160
be a huge scoop for the occult club?

00:17:01.530 --> 00:17:03.850
That stuff is too much for me to handle.

00:17:03.850 --> 00:17:06.830
We can't make news fodder out 
of this just for fun, can we?

00:17:09.500 --> 00:17:11.060
<i>What is this?</i>

00:17:14.070 --> 00:17:16.840
<i>I feel like I've seen this before...</i>

00:17:17.120 --> 00:17:18.130
What's wrong, Kotarou?

00:17:18.130 --> 00:17:19.270
You're sweating really badly.

00:17:19.270 --> 00:17:21.470
If you're tired, let's rest a little.

00:17:21.470 --> 00:17:23.610
Uh, no, I'm fine—

00:17:27.480 --> 00:17:28.490
It's her!

00:17:29.150 --> 00:17:29.980
Kotarou?!

00:17:44.300 --> 00:17:46.870
I never thought you'd follow me
all the way out here—

00:18:11.560 --> 00:18:14.320
Kotarou-kun! Kotarou-kun!

00:18:21.170 --> 00:18:22.530
What was that?!

00:18:22.770 --> 00:18:24.040
Kotarou!

00:18:24.040 --> 00:18:25.160
Kotarou!

00:18:25.790 --> 00:18:27.290
Kotarou-kun, this way is—

00:18:28.790 --> 00:18:30.270
A-Are you okay?

00:18:30.270 --> 00:18:32.560
You look pale.

00:18:32.560 --> 00:18:34.800
Y-Yeah, I'm fine.

00:18:36.600 --> 00:18:38.550
Sorry, let's head back.

00:18:39.430 --> 00:18:40.520
Yeah...

00:18:50.490 --> 00:18:52.040
What are you doing?

00:18:52.040 --> 00:18:54.070
Right back at you!

00:18:55.740 --> 00:18:58.960
I was feeling restless at home,

00:18:58.960 --> 00:19:02.200
so I figured I'd at least write down
what happened this afternoon,

00:19:02.200 --> 00:19:04.080
even though I don't intend to publish it.

00:19:05.760 --> 00:19:07.500
All right, done!

00:19:07.500 --> 00:19:08.760
Twenty points.

00:19:09.650 --> 00:19:13.520
After what we saw, "Chemicals that 
damage the environment are bad"

00:19:13.520 --> 00:19:15.670
is a very simple conclusion.

00:19:15.670 --> 00:19:17.620
If we're being honest,

00:19:17.620 --> 00:19:21.970
environmental damage is inevitable 
with lots of humans around, isn't it?

00:19:22.250 --> 00:19:24.100
There's nothing we can do about it.

00:19:24.800 --> 00:19:25.850
You're right.

00:19:26.110 --> 00:19:28.280
Accelerating environmental destruction.

00:19:28.280 --> 00:19:30.270
Resources on the verge of exhaustion.

00:19:30.270 --> 00:19:33.710
And yet a segment of humanity continues 
to indulge in their pleasures

00:19:33.710 --> 00:19:36.110
without any sense of impending danger.

00:19:36.560 --> 00:19:37.360
Yeesh.

00:19:37.920 --> 00:19:40.610
I wonder what they plan 
to do when the day comes?

00:19:41.550 --> 00:19:42.490
"The day"?

00:19:45.490 --> 00:19:47.740
The point of no return.

00:19:49.160 --> 00:19:52.480
It refers to the instant in time past which
we can no longer turn back.

00:19:52.850 --> 00:19:56.650
The day the Earth is beyond saving
isn't all that far away.

00:19:57.000 --> 00:19:59.010
You mean, humanity will go extinct?

00:19:59.490 --> 00:20:02.380
Unless we migrate to another planet.

00:20:03.240 --> 00:20:04.390
That's science fiction.

00:20:04.390 --> 00:20:05.640
How long

00:20:06.850 --> 00:20:09.520
do all of you plan to keep on dreaming?

00:20:10.890 --> 00:20:12.510
I-I...

00:20:13.490 --> 00:20:14.980
What are you scared for?

00:20:14.980 --> 00:20:16.020
How foolish.

00:20:16.430 --> 00:20:19.320
Why did you decide to write 
this down in the first place?

00:20:19.320 --> 00:20:21.900
Hoping to find a job in
an environmental organization?

00:20:22.100 --> 00:20:23.920
It's nothing that serious.

00:20:23.920 --> 00:20:24.490
It's just...

00:20:26.590 --> 00:20:31.250
I <i>do</i> believe there are people 
truly trying to protect the world.

00:20:31.250 --> 00:20:34.370
I didn't think it would hurt 
to at least do what I can.

00:20:36.040 --> 00:20:37.960
In that case, I know of a good method.

00:20:37.960 --> 00:20:38.670
Huh?

00:20:38.670 --> 00:20:40.930
Get rid of the source of the pollution.

00:20:40.930 --> 00:20:43.110
Oh, like factories and stuff?

00:20:43.110 --> 00:20:44.270
Not that.

00:20:44.270 --> 00:20:46.020
The answer is very simple.

00:20:46.020 --> 00:20:46.800
Huh?

00:20:47.060 --> 00:20:48.920
Just get rid of the humans.

00:21:00.510 --> 00:21:03.050
Sleep isn't making my fatigue go away.

00:21:05.510 --> 00:21:06.840
Hello?

00:21:06.840 --> 00:21:08.330
<i>This is Inoue.</i>

00:21:08.330 --> 00:21:10.700
<i>The occult club went to investigate 
the forest yesterday, didn't it?</i>

00:21:10.960 --> 00:21:11.820
Hey, Inoue.

00:21:11.820 --> 00:21:14.230
Do you have me wiretapped or something?

00:21:14.230 --> 00:21:15.500
<i>I would never!</i>

00:21:15.500 --> 00:21:16.920
<i>I just have a world-class spy—</i>

00:21:17.640 --> 00:21:19.110
Hey, what'd you just say?!

00:21:19.110 --> 00:21:23.360
<i>Did your investigation have to do with 
the Rainbow Swamp, by any chance?</i>

00:21:23.360 --> 00:21:24.730
Rainbow Swamp?

00:21:24.730 --> 00:21:26.500
<i>That's what I call it.</i>

00:21:26.500 --> 00:21:28.110
I see. That fits.

00:21:28.110 --> 00:21:30.300
We suspended the investigation, though.

00:21:30.720 --> 00:21:32.060
It was too heavy for us.

00:21:32.060 --> 00:21:33.240
<i>True.</i>

00:21:33.240 --> 00:21:35.320
<i>Given what's causing it,
this would fall into our territory.</i>

00:21:35.320 --> 00:21:36.600
Do you know something?

00:21:37.720 --> 00:21:39.950
<i>I got my hands on some juicy intel.</i>

00:21:39.950 --> 00:21:42.380
<i>I was thinking of going to
check out the forest.</i>

00:21:42.380 --> 00:21:43.860
What's this intel you got?

00:21:44.020 --> 00:21:46.760
<i>You'll have to wait and check
 the next front page to find out!</i>

00:21:46.760 --> 00:21:47.740
Yeah, yeah.

00:21:48.000 --> 00:21:49.800
Well, be careful, anyway.

00:21:49.800 --> 00:21:50.740
<i>Thanks.</i>

00:21:50.740 --> 00:21:51.750
<i>See ya!</i>

00:21:52.870 --> 00:21:53.620
Now, then...

00:21:55.080 --> 00:21:55.920
Who is it?!

00:21:55.920 --> 00:21:57.370
Who's the spy?!

00:21:58.880 --> 00:22:01.060
You're Tennouji-kun, right?

00:22:02.180 --> 00:22:03.420
I am. Why?

00:22:03.420 --> 00:22:05.690
Um, I'm from the newspaper club.

00:22:06.050 --> 00:22:08.170
I heard you're close to Inoue?

00:22:08.750 --> 00:22:10.200
I'm not sure you'd call us close.

00:22:10.200 --> 00:22:12.980
More like she messes with me...

00:22:12.980 --> 00:22:16.500
Oh, that reminds me. She called me on Sunday.

00:22:17.060 --> 00:22:19.050
Really? What did she say?!

00:22:19.050 --> 00:22:19.840
Huh?

00:22:19.840 --> 00:22:21.400
That she was about to head to the forest...

00:22:22.370 --> 00:22:26.030
Inoue hasn't come home for the 
past three days, since Sunday!

00:22:26.200 --> 00:22:26.920
What?!
